t solution scaffold\",\n      \"justification\": \"The fifteen captured source exercises use these two response forms. q-128198 must not disappear because the old snapshot had fourteen exercises.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"feature\": \"Nonzero/domain assumptions and local branches\",\n      \"justification\": \"Division by g(y) requires g(y) nonzero. Real root branches must be valid, but necessary assumptions do not justify printing the integrated answer in the question.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"answer_roles\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"Coefficient signs and resulting primitive/exponent\",\n      \"eligible_variation\": \"Signed small coefficients and constant/linear polynomial h(x), with all solutions and keys following the change.\",\n      \"observed\": \"Both easy templates cover a=-12..-1,1..12. The actual batch uses easy_linear a=3,12,-4,-1,1 and requires both exponent signs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"Which complete bank expression is correct\",\n      \"eligible_variation\": \"Vary coefficients/primitive terms and option order without preserving a cue that bypasses integration.\",\n      \"observed\": \"Fresh seeds change positions. Normal q-79665 and q-8304 put the entire correct inner expression in the interval restriction; the same copy-and-power action stays correct across coefficient changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"Blank scaffold and missing power\",\n      \"eligible_variation\": \"Both y=-2(blank+K)^(-1) and y=±(blank+K)^(1/2) source routes; vary missing expression coherently.\",\n      \"observed\": \"Only q-128191 is supported, with powers 2..5. q-128198 is rejected. New normal wording bans constant shifts even though original arbitrary-K families admit them.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"coverage\": [\n    {\n      \"case\": \"Independent easy sign/boundary grid and natural sampler control\",\n      \"sample_refs\": [\n        \"easy-grid.json\",\n        \"fresh-seed-samples.json\",\n        \"coverage-results.json\",\n        \"fresh-seed