{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1570,1625p' /home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/engine/rust/symbolic.rs; cat retained-regressions.log; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor f in ['batch.json','source-replay-results.json','regression-evidence/grader-report.json']:\n d=json.load(open(f));print(f,str(d)[:1600])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"        conditions.remove(&Condition::Nonzero(v.num.monic()));\n    }\n    Ok(Answer::Expression(value, conditions))\n}\n\n/// Whether a canonical answer has a bounded, supported representation.\npub fn supports(source: &str, context: Context) -> bool {\n    parse(source, context).is_ok()\n}\n\n/// Compare the expression before an explicitly displayed arbitrary +C.\n/// An exact, variable-free real difference is absorbed by that constant.\n/// Domain restrictions must still match; this does not prove identities by\n/// numerical sampling or turn ordinary expression equality into family equality.\npub fn compare_up_to_constant(a: &str, b: &str, context: Context) -> Result<bool> {\n    fn constant_poly(p: &Poly) -> bool {\n        p.0.keys().all(|mono| mono.keys().all(|atom| match atom {\n            Atom::Pi | Atom::E => true,\n            Atom::Root(_, p) => constant_poly(p),\n            Atom::Function(_, v) => constant_value(v),\n            Atom::Power(base, exponent) => constant_value(base) && constant_value(exponent),\n            Atom::Variable(_) | Atom::I => false,\n        }))\n    }\n    fn constant_value(v: &Value) -> bool {\n        constant_poly(&v.num) && constant_poly(&v.den)\n    }\n    if let (Answer::Expression(av, ac), Answer::Expression(bv, bc)) =\n        (parse(a, context)?, parse(b, context)?)\n    {\n        let mut algebra = Algebra {\n            work: 0, depth: 0, conditions: BTreeSet::new(),\n            nonzero_power_bases: BTreeMap::new(), context,\n        };\n        let difference = algebra.add(&av, &bv.neg())?;\n        if constant_value(&difference) {\n            if ac != bc {\n                return Err(\"antiderivative comparison has unresolved domain differences\".into());\n            }\n            return Ok(true);\n        }\n        // Literal inequality is insufficient here: a nonzero constant is a\n        // valid family difference. Two disjoint exact interval evaluations\n        // instead prove that the difference actually varies. As with ordinary\n        // comparison, samples can reject; they can never establish acceptance.\n        let mut intervals: Vec<(Q, Q)> = vec![];\n        for sample in counterexample_samples() {\n            if !ac.iter().chain(bc.iter()).all(|c| condition_at(c, &sample)) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            if let Some((lo, hi)) = difference.interval_at(Some(&sample)) {\n                if intervals.iter().any(|(a, b)| hi < *a || lo > *b) {\n                    return Ok(false);\n                }\n                intervals.push((lo, hi));\n            }\nmissing-family regression: 6 records, both signs pass\nshortcut regression: old defect detected; 0 leaks in 12 raw / 12 delivered\ngrading regression: exact retained counterexample, 10 current blank records, 6 negative contexts pass\nrendering regression: 5 actual UI pages, no literal mathematical code blocks; screenshots require author inspection\nbatch.json [{'knowledge_point': {'db_id': 17592186068841, 'id': '74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9', 'title': 'Finding General Solutions by Rearranging Then Integrating'}, 'question': {':question/id': '1918ecd2-43c4-5951-8f2b-713d370ba8a2', ':question/difficulty': ':question.difficulty/easy', ':question/problem': \"Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+3 xy=0$ for $y\\\\ne0.$\", ':question/worked-solution': \"To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}y'+3 xy=0 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}+3 xy & =0 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =- 3 xy \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =- 3 x\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int (- 3 x)\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\ \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\,\\\\text{d}y & =\\\\int (- 3 x)\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\ \\\\ln|y| & =- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\ln|y|=- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\ln|y| & =- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C \\\\\\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}+C} \\\\\\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}\\\\cdot e^C \\\\\\\\ |y| & =K e^{- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\\n\\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\\n\\n$$\\ny=K e^{- \\\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2}}.\\n\nsource-replay-results.json [{'source_id': '679701a5-b0c3-5865-adfd-e49e046da668', 'template': 'q-8303', 'prompt_exact': True, 'solution_exact': True, 'status': 'generated'}, {'source_id': 'b946e806-cd3a-503b-8b7c-fe17b0906080', 'template': 'q-8305', 'prompt_exact': True, 'solution_exact': True, 'status': 'generated'}, {'source_id': '778dd5ee-c1ff-5286-be7b-93fe7ada6aaf', 'template': 'q-128191', 'prompt_exact': False, 'solution_exact': True, 'status': 'generated'}, {'source_id': '8f251269-fa35-5ece-9af4-5538cedc8207', 'template': 'q-14247', 'prompt_exact': True, 'solution_exact': True, 'status': 'generated'}, {'source_id': 'de6a882e-022d-59c5-adf8-2e2394047b45', 'template': 'q-14253', 'prompt_exact': True, 'solution_exact': True, 'status': 'generated'}, {'source_id': 'e0c7db14-c9c5-588a-b927-09334c1e0842', 'template': 'q-158009', 'prompt_exact': True, '