s [\"First-order separable equations with elementary antiderivatives; no initial-value fitting, integrating factors or nonseparable equations.\", \"Preserve source radio versus blank response contract and complete distractor families at replay.\", \"Preserve nonzero/domain/branch assumptions. Nonzero exponential solutions require nonzero K.\", \"Requested easy difficulty has no captured easy exercise: canonical polynomial example is the nearest conservative difficulty anchor; do not relabel inverse-trigonometric/involved power forms easy.\"]\npermitted_variations [\"Change signed small coefficients, linear/quadratic monomial powers and additive terms while retaining the same integration method and workload.\", \"Change the coefficient sign so the antiderivative/exponent/denominator must change, rather than preserving a sign pattern as an incidental answer cue.\", \"For supported trigonometric families vary supported sine/cosine roles and signs with dependent antiderivatives; for shifted y family vary the shift coherently.\", \"Vary which bank member is correct and its position; do not fix a uniquely recognizable expression shape unless it follows from the intended mathematics.\", \"Vary the missing polynomial term/coefficient in source blank scaffolds; x^2 is an example assignment, not an invariant.\", \"The positive branch in q-79666 follows y>0; changing a valid branch assumption must change the explicit answer.\"]\nsource_refs [\"canonical e-10833 / 23d66cc8-8e5a-5a33-a7a1-c43f5facdcbc: y\\u2032+2xy=0, ln|y|=-x^2+C, y=Ke^{-x^2}\", \"tutorial 6767 / 56fc1c96-3599-5022-8d83-60d4188ccf07: dy/dx=h(x)g(y); separated (1/g(y))dy/dx=h(x); require g(y) != 0\", \"tutorial 6766 / dfb65111-b319-54c6-84cc-f60506595a69: separate e^{x-y}, integrate e^y=e^x+C, explicit y=ln(e^x+C)\"]\nsource_cases [{\"id\": \"679701a5-b0c3-5865-adfd-e49e046da668\", \"ma_id\": \"q-8303\", \"difficulty\": \":question.difficulty/moderate\", \"prompt\": \"Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{\\u2032}-\\\\sqrt{y}=2x\\\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\\\ne 0.$\", \"fields\": [{\":answer-field/choices\": [{\":answer/id\": \"121b603b-942f-556e-b445-2d681ee1ce18\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y={\\\\left(\\\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2}\\\\right)}^{2}\", \":db/id\": 17592186348602}, {\":answer/id\": \"500546dd-32e0-5461-ae4c-5e5a7455b919\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y={x}^{2}+x+C\", \":db/id\": 17592186349173}, {\":answer/id\": \"6e22fd1e-737c-5a35-9366-28fb7f8a36bc\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y=({x}^{2}+x)^{2}\", \":db/id\": 17592186349458}, {\":answer/id\": \"da4666f1-e8ca-5840-a41a-ead889cfbef8\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y=({x}^{2}+x+C)^{2}\", \":db/id\": 17592186350361}, {\":answer/id\": \"f06bf25f-3d03-5f76-a7ea-8ddc6224884a\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y={\\\\left(\\\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{2}\\\\right)}^{2}\", \":db/id\": 17592186350551}], \":answer-field/correct\": {\":answer/id\": \"121b603b-942f-556e-b445-2d681ee1ce18\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y={\\\\left(\\\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2}\\\\right)}^{2}\", \":db/id\": 17592186348602}, \":answer-field/id\": \"8e1d264b-d2af-5bb5-bbc0-5706b21c43ca\", \":answer-field/key\": \"selection\", \":answer-field/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer-field.type/radio\"}, \":db/id\": 17592186350948}], \"worked_solution\": \"To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\\u2032}-\\\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\\\sqrt{y} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}-\\\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\\\sqrt{y} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =2x\\\\sqrt{y}+\\\\sqrt{y} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\\\sqrt{y} \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{y}}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{y}}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int (2x+1)\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\ \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{y}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}y & =\\\\int (2x+1)\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\ 2\\\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\\n$$\\n\\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\\\left(\\\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2}\\\\right)}^{2}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"}, {\"id\": \"b946e806-cd3a-503b-8b7c-fe17b0906080\", \"ma_id\": \"q-8305\", \"difficulty\": \":question.difficulty/hard\", \"prompt\": \"Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}-(\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x)y=0$ for $y\\\\ne 0.$\", \"fields\": [{\":answer-field/choices\": [{\":answer/id\": \"610604c1-be04-5ae1-8759-b50654e72419\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y=K{e}^{-\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x}\", \":db/id\": 17592186349333}, {\":answer/id\": \"6b4f4cea-17dd-5832-b0a8-70627738c306\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y={e}^{-\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x}+K\", \":db/id\": 17592186349434}, {\":answer/id\": \"6c66c47e-a365-5d7e-8cc6-1deb04431c20\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y={e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x}+K\", \":db/id\": 17592186349447}, {\":answer/id\": \"759561ba-3f4a-5157-8283-98918b52bdbb\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y=K{e}^{\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x}\", \":db/id\": 17592186349529}, {\":answer/id\": \"dc2e52a7-5613-5624-ab39-0ecff616a3c4\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y=K{e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x}\", \":db/id\": 17592186350372}], \":answer-field/correct\": {\":answer/id\": \"dc2e52a7-5613-5624-ab39-0ecff616a3c4\", \":answer/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer.type/math\"}, \":answer/value\": \"y=K{e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x}\", \":db/id\": 17592186350372}, \":answer-field/id\": \"26a2711c-7312-535e-b8ec-1d2da18482c4\", \":answer-field/key\": \"selection\", \":answer-field/type\": {\":db/ident\": \":answer-field.type/radio\"}, \":db/id\": 17592186350780}], \"worked_solution\": \"To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}-(\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x)y & =0 \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =(\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x)y \\\\\\\\ \\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x} & =\\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}y}{\\\\text{d}x}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\ \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{y}\\\\,\\\\text{d}y & =\\\\int \\\\operatorname{cos}\\u2061x\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\ \\\\operatorname{ln}\\u2061|y| & =\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\operatorname{ln}\\u2061|y|=\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x+C.\\n$$\\n\\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\operatorname{ln}\\u2061|y| & =\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x+C \\\\\\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x+C} \\\\\\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x}\\\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\\\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\\n\\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\\n\\n$$\\ny=K{e}^{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\u2061x}.\\n$$\"}, {\"id\": \"778dd5ee-c1ff-5286-be7b-93fe7ada6aaf\", \"ma_id\": \"q-128191\", \"difficulty\": \":question.difficulty/moderate\", \"prompt\": \"Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{\\u2032}=x{y}^{2}.$ Assume that $y\\\\ne 0$ and $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\\n\\n                            \\n                                    \\n                                        \\n                                            \\n\\n                                                \\n\\n                                        \\n                                        \\n                                        \\n\\n                                    \\n                                \\n                                    \\n                                        \\n                                        $y=-2($ \\n\\n                                    \\n                                \\n                                    \\n                            \\n                                        {{field-1}}                \\n                                    \\n                                \\n                                    \\n                                        \\n                                        $+K)^{-1}$\", \"fields\": [{\":answer-field/choices\": [{\":answer/id\": \"f680649b-aad0-5c21-b454-2962d171cc58\", \":answer\nsource_gaps [\"No source images; no prerequisite entries; surrounding lesson and adjacent canonical examples supply method context.\", \"No easy-labeled source exercise.\", \"q-79665 and q-8304 split sqrt(xy) without explicit positivity, omitting negative x,y real branches; q-8303 squaring requires local nonnegative unsquared expression. These need documented domain corrections, not blind reproduction.\"]\nmaterial keys ['kp', 'topics', 'lessons', 'prerequisites', 'images']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
