{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat math-command.log\ncat /home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186068841/review-0-policy-2-75766812ae9ead5b/run_delivery.py\ncat /home/jake/.codex/skills/just-say-no-to-process-porn-and-ceremony/SKILL.md'","aggregated_output":"bank 15 failures []\nmath 59 failures [{'file': 'normal-cases.json', 'index': 28, 'id': '1131efeb-235b-534a-a924-e25df3cc1931', 'passed': False, 'error': 'ValueError(\"Unknown token \\',\\'\")'}, {'file': 'normal-cases.json', 'index': 29, 'id': '0db990ed-45ff-5aa0-92c2-ebd9ad256f2a', 'passed': False, 'error': 'ValueError(\"Unknown token \\',\\'\")'}]\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess,json,sys\nr=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;j=r.parent;repo=Path('/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy');py=str(repo/'.venv/bin/python')\ncommands=[]\nfor file,difficulty,name in [('batch.json','easy','delivery-batch'),('easy-grid.json','easy','delivery-easy'),('moderate-delivery-input.json','moderate','delivery-moderate'),('hard-delivery-input.json','hard','delivery-hard')]:\n cmd=[py,str(repo/'generate/pipeline/check_delivery.py'),'--input',str(r/file),'--source',str(j/'source/source.json'),'--inventory',str(j/'source/inventory.json'),'--difficulty',difficulty,'--output',str(r/name),'--asset-root',str(r)]\n p=subprocess.run(cmd,capture_output=True,text=True);commands.append({'command':cmd,'returncode':p.returncode,'stdout':p.stdout,'stderr':p.stderr});print(name,p.returncode,p.stdout.strip(),p.stderr[-300:])\n(r/'delivery-commands.json').write_text(json.dumps(commands,indent=2))\n---\nname: just-say-no-to-process-porn-and-ceremony\ndescription: Detect and stop process porn, ceremony, reward hacking, and finish-line avoidance by coding agents or swarms. Use when work looks busy but little is shipping, when auditing agent honesty, or before declaring completion.\n---\n\n# Just Say No to Process Porn and Ceremony\n\n## Purpose\n\nKeep agents focused on changing reality, not producing evidence of busyness.\n\n**Outcome > activity. Evidence > confidence. Shipping > ceremony.**\n\nPlanning, coordination, review, and documentation are useful only when they enable execution, reduce meaningful uncertainty, satisfy a real constraint, or verify the result.\n\n## When this triggers\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- agents are producing lots of plans, status, reviews, handoffs, trackers, or summaries;\n- many subtasks are “complete” but the requested outcome still does not work;\n- progress claims are stronger than their evidence;\n- agents are optimizing task counts, green metrics, praise, or completion language;\n- work repeatedly reaches “almost done” without crossing the finish line;\n- you are about to tell the user the work is complete.\n\n## The rule\n\nAsk one question repeatedly:\n\n> What is the next action that materially changes or verifies the user's requested outcome?\n\nIf you know the answer, do that instead of creating more process.\n\n## Fast audit\n\nRun these three checks. Keep the answers short.\n\n### 1. Reward hacking / honesty\n\n- What are we claiming is done?\n- What concrete evidence supports each important claim?\n- Did we weaken acceptance criteria, cherry-pick evidence, inflate task counts, or call partial work complete?\n- Which claims need to be retracted or downgraded?\n\nReality wins over the scoreboard.\n\n### 2. Process / ceremony\n\nLook at current activity and ask:\n\n- Does this directly change the product or verified state?\n- Does it unblock that work?\n- Does it provide necessary assurance?\n\nIf none apply, stop it.\n\nCommon waste: recursive planning, trackers for trackers, review-of-review loops, status fan-out, summary agents, duplicated workstreams, and spawning agents merely to look parallel.\n\n### 3. Finish-line avoidance\n\n- What acceptance criterion is still unmet?\n- What uncomfortable or difficult step are we avoiding?\n- What is the shortest action that moves that criterion toward verified completion?\n\nDo that action now when possible.\n\n## Evidence language\n\nMatch wording to evidence:\n\n- **Implemented** — the change exists.\n- **Verified** — a relevant check was actually run and passed.\n- **Fixed** — the original failure is addressed and relevant regression evidence passes.\n- **Deployed** — deployment actually happened and the target state was observed.\n- **Likely / appears** — evidence is incomplete.\n- **Unknown** — you do not know.\n\nNever invent test results, deployments, verification, or certainty.\n\n## Swarms\n\nParallelism is useful only when it shortens the path to the outcome.\n\n- Give agents disjoint, outcome-bearing work.\n- Do not create agents whose main job is summarizing other agents.\n- Stop duplicate or low-value workstreams.\n- Keep one clear owner for integration and final verification.\n- Do not count agents, messages, or subtasks as progress.\n\n## Before saying “done”\n\n1. Re-read the user's actual objective.\n2. Check every material acceptance criterion against evidence.\n3. Run relevant validation when possible.\n4. State remaining failures or uncertainty plainly.\n5. If something important is unfinished and you can still act, keep working instead of writing a completion speech.\n\n## Intervention style\n\nWhen you catch ceremony, do not write an essay about ceremony.\n\nState only:\n\n- **Actual state:** what is demonstrably done and not done.\n- **Stop:** the wasteful activity being dropped.\n- **Next:** the highest-value state-changing action.\n- **Proof:** what will demonstrate completion.\n\nThen act.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- Do not substitute plans for implementation.\n- Do not substitute documentation of a fix for the fix itself.\n- Do not repeatedly re-plan when the next concrete action is already known.\n- Do not weaken the user's requirements to manufacture success.\n- Do not hide known failures behind percentages or upbeat summaries.\n- Do not add ceremony just because a framework normally contains it.\n- Keep genuinely required safety, regulatory, migration, or organizational process—but no more than necessary.\n- **Do not turn this skill into ceremony. Once the problem is identified, stop auditing and do the work.**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
