l': 'fresh-independent-1', 'template': 'eas\nFind the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y},$ given that $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y=\\pm ($ {{field-1}} $+K)^{1/2}$\nFirst, we separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2C \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+K \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+K} \\\\ y & =\\pm ({x}^{2}+K)^{1/2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary constant.\nFind the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{8x}{y},$ given that $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n$y=\\pm ($ {{field-1}} $+K)^{1/2}$\nFirst, we separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{8x}{y} \\\\ y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =4{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =8{x}^{2}+2C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =8{x}^{2}+K \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{8{x}^{2}+K} \\\\ y & =\\pm (8{x}^{2}+K)^{1/2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
