{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"Independent checks pass for all 15 source banks, the restored blank family’s two branches, and 56 valid plus 96 invalid native-grader submissions. All five batch records survive filtering; they vary coefficients and signs, and the tested cues do not answer the whole batch. The inspected screenshots also show the repaired blanks as mathematics, with no answer leakage in the revised domain wording.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > finish_review.py <<'PY'\nimport sys,json,re,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsys.dont_write_bytecode=True\nE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;J=E.parent;P=J/'workspace'\ndef load(n):return json.loads((E/n).read_text())\ndef save(n,v):(E/n).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\n# Source prompt normalization is a content check, not a waiver based on the author's claim.\nsrc=json.loads((J/'source/source.json').read_text())['material']['kp'][':knowledge-point/questions'];by={q[':question/math-academy-id']:q for q in src}\nreplay=load('source-replay.json');rows=[]\nfor r in replay:\n name=r['generation']['template'];q=by[name];out=r['question'];rows.append({'template':name,'source_id':q[':question/id'],'prompt_equal_ignoring_whitespace':re.sub(r'\\\\s+','',out[':question/problem'])==re.sub(r'\\\\s+','',q[':question/problem']),'solution_exact':out[':question/worked-solution']==q[':question/worked-solution'],'response_type_preserved':out[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/type']==q[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/type'][':db/ident'],'full_bank_evidence':'source-bank-comparison.json'})\nassert all(x['prompt_equal_ignoring_whitespace'] and x['solution_exact'] and x['response_type_preserved'] for x in rows)\nsave('source-normalization.json',rows)\n# Explicit inventory metadata differences, rather than claiming exact provenance identity.\nold=json.loads((P/'17592186068841/reference/replenishment/basis-2684/generated.json').read_text());fresh=load('generated-records.json');inventory=load('inventory-reproduction.json')\nfor row,a,b in zip(inventory['reproduced'],old,fresh):row['generation_differences']={k:{'captured':v,'current':b['generation'].get(k)} for k,v in a['generation'].items() if b['generation'].get(k)\"'!=v}\nassert all(x['\"'matched'] for x in inventory['reproduced']);save('inventory-reproduction.json',inventory)\n# Save actual renderer structure and observations after personally viewing representative screenshots.\nrender=load('fresh-render/rendering.json');assert render['passed'] and len(render['cases'])==19\nstruct=[]\nfor i in range(1,20):\n html=(E/f'fresh-render/question-{i:03}.html').read_text();blocks=re.findall(r'<pre.*?</pre>',html,re.S);assert not blocks\n struct.append({'index':i,'code_blocks':0,'mathjax':bool(re.search('mjx-container',html))})\nsave('rendering-inspection.json',{'actual_renderer':'unmodified Learning.html and learning.js; render_preview.py --limit 19','all_records':struct,'visually_inspected':['fresh-render/question-001.png','author-rerun/render/question-003.png','fresh-render/question-007.png','fresh-render/question-009.png','author-rerun/render/question-005.png'],'observations':['Batch radio prompt, all five choices and full logarithmic/exponential worked solution legible.','New square-root blank is in line between ±( and +K)\"'^(1/2), including a=8; both sign branches appear in solution.'\"','Power-rule blank at a=4 displays x\"'^5 and complete consistent worked denominator; no literal Markdown code.'\"','Repaired radical prompt states local positive branch without printing the computed primitive; computed restriction appears only in worked solution.'],'errors':[]})\n# All executable results checked, not just exit codes.\nassert all(x['passed'] for x in load('math-results.json')['records'])\nassert all(x['bank_match'] and x['key_match'] for x in load('source-bank-comparison.json'))\nassert all(x['passed'] for x in load('counterfactual-results.json'))\nassert all(x['final_matches_key'] and all(z['passes'] for z in x['differentiation']) for x in load('pair-math.json'))\nassert load('fresh-grader-command.json')['returncode']==0\nassert 'old defect detected' in (E/'author-rerun-command.log').read_text()\n# Pedagogical account challenges roles independently and keeps historical failures separate.\nprobes=load('shortcut-probes.json')\nfor file in ['batch.json','fresh-samples.json','delivery-fresh/accepted.json']:\n rows2=load(file.replace('.json','-sign-cue.json'))\n for name in sorted(set(r['generation']['template'] for r in load(file))):\n  sub=[x for x,r in zip(rows2,load(file)) if r['generation']['template']==name]\n  assert all(x['candidate_count']>=2 and x['contains_key'] for x in sub)\n  probes.append({'cue':'sign of exponential factor','subgroup':file+':'+name,'scope':'within_template','strategy':'Choose the unique multiplicative exponential having the expected sign, without computing the primitive','correct':0,'total':len(sub),'baseline':0.2,'disposition':'not_predictive','conclusion':'Opposite-sign knowledge expresses rearrangement, but does not determine the option: at least two candidates remain for every record. Correct counts measure unique successful action. Baseline is random choice among five.','sample_refs':[file,file.replace('.json','-sign-cue.json')]})\n# Context-specific invariant shapes are legitimate partial mathematics, rather than incidental answer labels.\nped={'learner_operation':load('source-analysis.json')['learner_operation'],\n'fixed_features':[{'feature':'First-order separable ODEs, elementary primitives, explicit general solutions','justification':'Tutorial 6767 requires separating dy/g(y)=h(x)dx; e-10833 integrates and solves explicitly. No initial values or integrating-factor method.'},{'feature':'Five-choice radio or explicit-solution scaffold with one blank','justification':'All 15 captured questions use these contracts. Scaffolds provide some algebra by design; missing expression still follows the printed ODE.'},{'feature':'Real local domains and branches','justification':'Tutorial 6767 requires g(y)≠0; roots require local valid branches. Such assumptions need not print their antiderivatives.'}],\n'answer_roles':[{'role':'Exponent coefficient and sign','eligible_variation':'Change signed coefficient and constant/linear x multiplier; derive exponent and choices together.','observed':'Both easy templates and coefficient signs occur in ordinary fresh seeds and survive delivery; independent boundaries include ±1 and ±12. Batch has five linear cases with three positive and two negative coefficients.'},{'role':'Missing polynomial power or coefficient','eligible_variation':'Vary which polynomial term fills the blank while retaining its explicit solution scaffold and arbitrary-constant freedom.','observed':'q-128191 changes x² to x⁵; restored q-128198 changes x² to 8x². Both source scaffolds remain supported, including ± branch. Constant shifts accepted without narrowing prompt.'},{'role':'Correct choice placement and distinguishing integration/inversion operation','eligible_variation':'Position may permute independently; mathematical primitive and distractors must respond to coefficient changes. Fixed root/exponential solution type follows g(y) and is legitimate partial knowledge, but must leave competing choices.','observed':'Current radical banks contain multiple candidates with the required power; interval-copy cue removed. Easy sign-only cue leaves ≥2 candidates. Position-only strategies are not perfect in the five-item batch or independent ordinary-seed subgroups.'}],\n'coverage':[{'case':'Source replay','sample_refs':['source-replay.json','source-normalization.json','source-bank-comparison.json'],'result':'All 15 prompts match ignoring captured whitespace; complete answer banks, keyed designations and exact worked templates replay. Observed domain/duplicate distractor errors remain evidence-only; served profiles correct them.'},{'case':'Exact requested easy batch','sample_refs':['batch.json','delivery-batch/accepted.json','coverage-results.json'],'result':'5/5 survive. All linear, with a=3,12,-4,-1,1; three magnitude levels beyond signs. Fixed-position and sign-only unique-choice attacks do not solve the batch. This five-item pool is narrow but valid practice of the canonical polynomial route, and is not claimed to cover every source route.'},{'case':'Independent boundaries and fresh natural seeds','sample_refs':['easy-grid.json','fresh-samples.json','coverage-results.json','delivery-fresh/accepted.json'],'result':'12 boundary controls across both templates; 9 survive inventory. Fresh seeds 942701..942716 give 16 records, 10 survivors, both templates and signs retained. Fixed grid intentionally reused one seed; its common position is an audit control, not natural sampling.'},{'case':'Changed source families and profiles','sample_refs':['normal-cases.json','author-rerun/family-records.json','leak-cases.json','delivery-moderate/accepted.json'],'result':'Default and upper boundary for every family, both public blank profiles at 1,2,8 for restored family. All three repaired radical families tested at 1,2,7,8; all twelve coefficient cases survive in the combined moderate delivery.'}],\n'counterfactuals':[], 'shortcut_probes':probes,\n'delivery':{'stages_examined':['generator bounds, complete-bank equivalence rejection and deterministic replay','requested-difficulty filtering','actual publisher normalization, validation and stable IDs','captured inventory and within-batch deduplication','freshness/history exclusion and difficulty-first learner selection rules'], 'sample_refs':['runtime.json','coverage-results.json','delivery-batch/delivery.json','delivery-fresh/delivery.json','delivery-moderate/delivery.json','delivery-hard/delivery.json','learner-selection.json','inventory-reproduction.json','generated-records.json','affected-inventory.json'],'result':'Batch 5→5; easy boundaries 12→9; fresh easy 16→10; moderate 30→24; hard 12→11. No cue reappears after filtering. Read-only selector reproduction uses exact SHA draw for positive-weight fresh pools; all surviving decisions remain reachable. Source snapshot basis 5369; six historical generated records reproduce and none belongs to retained defective families. No publication preparation exists; no database writes.'},\n'limitations':['Finite review does not prove absence of every shortcut.','Actual future learner policy, numeric entity ordering and histories are unavailable. Selection counts are illustrative under explicit positive-weight fresh-learner conditions; structural selection behavior inspected including zero-weight and no-policy fallback.','Captured inventory basis 5369 can change.','No easy-labeled exercise is captured: easy variants are conservative authored extensions of canonical e-10833.','Unchanged construction rules were sampled and prior analysis reused rather than exhaustively re-audited.']}\nfor x in load('counterfactual-results.json'):\n ped['counterfactuals'].append({'kind':x['kind'],'change':x['template']+(': coefficient/power or sign changed with seed held fixed' if x['kind']=='relevant' else ': seed and option order changed, printed ODE held fixed'),'expected':'Prompt, solution and mathematical response change coherently' if x['kind']=='relevant' else 'Prompt, solution and response preserved despite choice reordering','observed':x['before_answer']+' → '+x['after_answer']+'. Native grader validates both, and rejects crossed old/new blank responses. Printed final solutions and independent differential residuals agree; both rendered.','status':'passed','justification':'Separation and integration in tutorial 6767 depend on the ODE coefficients, not option order. Blank scaffolds are source-supported.','sample_refs':['pairs.json','counterfactual-results.json','pair-math.json','fresh-grader-input.json','fresh-grader-report.json','fresh-render-input.json','fresh-render/rendering.json']})\nsave('pedagogical-variation.json',ped)\n# Read-only scope account tied to actual records and historical fixes.\nsave('scope-results.json',{'source_basis':'source-analysis.json','records':'normal-cases.json','repaired_families':['q-128198 restored with source scaffold and both sign branches; no new prerequisite','q-128191 nonconstant-only prompt removed; arbitrary-K constant shifts retained','q-8303/q-79665/q-8304 local-branch restriction preserved without exposing antiderivatives'],'easy':'Small signed constant or linear x factors in y′+h(x)y=0. Canonical e-10833 uses 2x, same separation/log/inversion sequence. Constant x factors simplify the same sequence.','source_corrections':'Observed sqrt(xy) examples omitted positivity; served version supplies x>0,y>0. Squared primitive valid only locally on positive unsquared branch. q-158009 false signed-K absolute-value row removed. q-3854 duplicate log distractor family repaired.','unsupported_source_families':[],'inference_limits':'Easy level is inferred conservatively from canonical example, not an observed easy exercise. Positive coefficient bounds in existing moderate/hard families retain same primitive workload; no claim that all possible separable ODEs are covered.'})\nbefore=load('package-before.json');after={str(p.relative_to(P)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in P.rglob('*') if p.is_file()};assert before==after\nsave('review-integrity.json',{'unchanged':True,'file_count':len(after),'changed_files':[k for k in set(before)|set(after) if before.get(k)\"'!=after.get(k)],'\"'writes':'Review scripts and outputs only under evidence_root; no package mutation, publishing or DB writes.','current_package_binding':'93cc5e18f727aad29c2363e48c2ecbd2a03f4a27ea2e4a885a6ac5fb57ae69ab','source_binding':'6bb5049e550d2f159ce463dacfff33d35112a586e169ddc01167b9221fee8ed2','engine_binding':'068e04ae69feec8bf48b25d41459cceb97bea9bdf34eac0d8efa255194293eea'})\nsa=load('source-analysis.json')\nchecks={\n'source_replay':(['source-normalization.json','source-bank-comparison.json','source-replay.json'],'All 15 source prompts, full answer banks, keys and solutions replay; captured blank whitespace normalized.'),\n'math':(['math-results.json','pair-math.json','independent_math.py'],'Independent printed-ODE differentiation passes 78 records; controlled-pair final solutions agree, including both restored square-root branches.'),\n'variety':(['coverage-results.json','normal-cases.json','fresh-samples.json','author-rerun/family-math.json'],'Restored source family and both blank profiles work. Signed easy boundaries, both easy templates and coefficient-dependent responses survive filtering.'),\n'scope':(['scope-results.json','normal-cases.json','source-analysis.json'],'Repairs preserve the source methods, response contracts and branch conditions. No nonconstant-only restriction remains.'),\n'grading':(['fresh-grader-input.json','fresh-grader-report.json','fresh-grader-command.json','author-rerun/grader-report.json','retained-failures.json'],'Native grading passes 56 valid and 96 invalid independent submissions, including the historical strict constant-shift case and cross-pair rejections. Retained author checks also pass.'),\n'rendering':(['rendering-inspection.json','fresh-render/rendering.json','fresh-render-input.json','fresh-render/question-007.png','fresh-render/question-009.png'],'Actual UI renders all 19 batch/counterfactual records; representative screenshots inspected. Blank scaffolds, controls and worked mathematics display correctly.'),\n'packaging':(['packaging-results.json','relocation-samples.json','review-integrity.json'],'Exact declared runtime versions match. Declared-file-only relocation, replay and invalid-input boundaries pass; package unchanged.'),\n'decision_variation':(['pedagogical-variation.json','counterfactual-results.json','coverage-results.json','learner-selection.json','affected-inventory.json','retained-failures.json'],'Relevant and irrelevant controlled pairs follow expected dependencies. Historical copy cue detected in old output and absent in current delivered cases. Exact batch passes tested position/sign strategies. All applicable delivery stages examined with captured-state limits.')}\nresult={'verdict':'accepted','summary':'All eight checks pass. The four retained defects are resolved in tested cases; the exact five-record batch survives filtering. Package files rema